# AQP Rate-Limit

- [aqp_ratelimit/](mdc:aqp_ratelimit/) owns the per-(user, service,
  key_id) rate-limit accounting subsystem: the
  [`IngestionRateLimitStrategy`](mdc:aqp_ratelimit/src/aqp_ratelimit/strategies/base.py)
  ABC + `IngestionRateLimitMeta` metaclass, every concrete strategy
  under [`strategies/`](mdc:aqp_ratelimit/src/aqp_ratelimit/strategies/),
  the Redis Lua token-bucket script
  ([`lua/token_bucket.lua`](mdc:aqp_ratelimit/lua/token_bucket.lua)),
  the Go RLS binary ([`go-rls/`](mdc:aqp_ratelimit/go-rls/)) speaking
  gRPC + REST, the Envoy descriptor filter
  ([`envoy/`](mdc:aqp_ratelimit/envoy/)), the Python sync + async
  clients ([`src/aqp_ratelimit/client.py`](mdc:aqp_ratelimit/src/aqp_ratelimit/client.py)),
  and the optional replay cache
  ([`src/aqp_ratelimit/replay_cache/`](mdc:aqp_ratelimit/src/aqp_ratelimit/replay_cache/)).
- Every concrete `IngestionRateLimitStrategy` registers via the
  [`IngestionRateLimitMeta`](mdc:aqp_ratelimit/src/aqp_ratelimit/strategies/base.py)
  metaclass. Set `strategy_kind` (one of `redis_token_bucket`,
  `in_memory`, `leaky_bucket`, `per_agent`, `replay_cache`) and
  `strategy_alias`. Don't decorate with `@register` manually.
- All bucket reads / decrements go through the strategy's
  `check()` / `reserve()` / `release()` methods. Never `HMGET`/`HSET`
  the Redis bucket key directly outside
  [`strategies/redis_token_bucket.py`](mdc:aqp_ratelimit/src/aqp_ratelimit/strategies/redis_token_bucket.py)
  — the Lua atomicity contract assumes it owns the key namespace
  `aqp:rl:{user_id}:{service}:{key_id}`.
- The `rl_policies`, `rl_keys`, `rl_ledger`, `user_tiers`,
  `template_catalog`, and `audit_log` Postgres tables are workspace-
  scoped and registered in [`aqp.tenancy.rls_policies.RLS_TABLES`](mdc:aqp/tenancy/rls_policies.py).
  ORM lives at [`aqp/persistence/models_ratelimit.py`](mdc:aqp/persistence/models_ratelimit.py).
  Migrations 0066-0069. Migrations are immutable once committed
  (root AGENTS.md rule 6).
- All four data.ratelimit.* MCP tools live at
  [`aqp/data/mcp/tools/ratelimit.py`](mdc:aqp/data/mcp/tools/ratelimit.py).
  Mutating tools (`data.ratelimit.reserve`, `data.ratelimit.policy.update`)
  set `mutates=True` and the matching FastAPI route attaches
  `Depends(require_step_up(max_age_seconds=180))` (root AGENTS.md rule 52).
- Every credential-resolution chokepoint that consumes vendor quota
  (Airbyte CDK `RateLimitedHttpStream`, `Fetcher._throttle`, Dagster
  asset sensors that gate partitioned backfills) MUST call the
  active strategy via the singleton client at
  [`get_ratelimit_client()`](mdc:aqp_ratelimit/src/aqp_ratelimit/client.py)
  — never inline a counter, never bypass.
- The Envoy forward-proxy is the inline enforcement mechanism for
  HTTP transports; non-HTTP transports (Bloomberg BPIPE,
  Refinitiv RFA) integrate at the Python SDK level by calling the
  same strategy client.
- The Lua script at
  [`lua/token_bucket.lua`](mdc:aqp_ratelimit/lua/token_bucket.lua)
  is the verbatim Redis token-bucket pattern from the blueprint;
  loaded once via `SCRIPT LOAD` and invoked via `EVALSHA` so the
  rate check sits on the synchronous request path without adding
  meaningful delay even at millions of QPS.
- Per-agent buckets (`strategy_kind="per_agent"`) sit alongside
  per-user buckets so an autonomous agent (root AGENTS.md rule 54)
  can never spend the user's budget without also drawing down its
  own small ceiling. The bridge in
  [`bridges/agent_bridge.py`](mdc:aqp_ratelimit/src/aqp_ratelimit/bridges/agent_bridge.py)
  reads `MCPToolContext.actor_kind="agent"` and dual-debits.

Validation:

```bash
cd aqp_ratelimit
pip install -e .
pytest -ra
ruff check src tests
cd go-rls && go test ./...
```
